---
import ServicePage from '../../components/services/ServicePage.astro';
import { SERVICES } from '../../data/site';

export const prerender = true;

const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/services/ai-agent-development';
const svc = SERVICES[0];

const FAQ = [
  {
    q: 'What if the AI gets something wrong?',
    a: 'I plan for it. Every agent gets clear limits that you approve before launch. Anything risky, like spending money, publishing or deleting, waits for a person to approve it. I test it on real examples from your business before it goes live.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which AI models do you use?',
    a: 'Whichever fits the job, usually Claude or GPT. I set things up so you can switch models later without starting over.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does an agent take to build?',
    a: "A working first version usually takes days. We pick one job, like lead follow-up, build that first and test it on real examples from your business. Then it gets better as real use shows what to fix.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Who owns the agent?',
    a: 'You do. The code, the instructions and the accounts it runs on are in your name. If we ever stop working together, everything stays with you.',
  },
];
---
<ServicePage
  title="Custom AI Agent Development Services | Neil Busque"
  description="Custom AI agents that work inside your CRM, inbox, calendar and database, with clear limits, approval steps and direct access to the person who builds them."
  canonical={canonical}
  heading="AI agent development for **growing businesses**."
  lead="I build agents that work inside the tools your team already uses. They answer leads, update the CRM, run research and draft replies, and anything risky waits for your OK."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/services' },
    { name: 'AI Agent Development', url: canonical },
  ]}
  topic="AI agent development"
  artSeed={svc.slug}
  artPalette="mist"
  summary={{ items: svc.items, facts: svc.facts }}
  related={['crm-with-ai-follow-up', 'ai-phone-receptionist-roofing']}
  relatedPalettes={['paper', 'navy']}
  faq={FAQ}
  service={{
    name: 'AI Agent Development Services',
    serviceType: ['AI agent development', 'LLM application development', 'MCP tool integration', 'AI automation'],
    areaServed: ['New Jersey', 'New York', 'New York City', 'United States', 'Remote'],
  }}
>
  <h2>What an AI agent actually is</h2>
  <p>A useful agent is more than a chat window. It reads a situation, chooses the next step and uses a small set of tools to finish the job. The difference is action: a chatbot answers, while an agent can update the systems where the work lives.</p>

  <h2>Agents I build</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Inbox and lead agents.</strong> Read what came in, sort it, look the person up, draft the reply, log it and pass the ones that need you.</li>
    <li><strong>CRM agents.</strong> Keep records clean, fill in missing details and move deals on real signals instead of someone remembering.</li>
    <li><strong>Phone and website agents.</strong> Answer, ask the right questions and book the appointment. More on <a href="/software/ai-phone-agent-for-business">AI phone agents</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Research agents.</strong> Pull sources on a schedule, summarize them and hand you a short brief instead of fifty open tabs.</li>
    <li><strong>Ops agents.</strong> Watch for a condition, do the steps that follow and tell you when they could not.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The stack</h2>
  <p>I usually build on Claude and connect the agent through MCP. That gives it controlled access to a CRM, inbox, calendar or database without wiring every tool into one app. The permissions and the shape of the job matter more than the model name.</p>

  <h2>Guardrails, because agents fail</h2>
  <p>Every agent needs a clear boundary. Reads can be broad when the data is safe. Writes stay limited to the job. Anything risky, like spending money, publishing or deleting, waits for a person to approve it. The goal is not pretending the agent will never make a mistake. It is making mistakes visible, easy to undo and cheap.</p>
  <p>My own CRM works this way: its assistant can take about 150 different actions in the app, and it asks before anything risky.</p>

  <h2>How the work runs</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>A first message or a short call.</strong> Which job are we handing over, and what is it allowed to touch.</li>
    <li><strong>A clear scope and price.</strong> In plain English, before anything is built.</li>
    <li><strong>A first version in days.</strong> Wired into your real systems, tested on real examples from your business.</li>
    <li><strong>Launch, then you choose.</strong> I keep it running and tune it each month, or hand it to your team.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Who you are working with</h2>
  <p>You work with me directly, from the first message to launch and after. I'm Neil Busque, based in New Jersey, and I work with teams across New Jersey, New York City and the rest of the US. I shipped more than 40 apps, agents and automations in 2026. See <a href="/work">the work</a>, read <a href="/guides/build-ai-agent-claude-code">how I build agents</a>, or see the wider picture in <a href="/services/ai-automation-services">AI automation services</a>.</p>
</ServicePage>
